that is, in ice dancing circles.

446
00:29:04,960 --> 00:29:06,359
简直是一坨垃圾。
This is rubbish.

447
00:29:10,280 --> 00:29:12,920
这儿多使点劲，别偷懒。
快点。
Work a bit harder here, don't be lazy.
Come on.

448
00:29:14,280 --> 00:29:16,556
来，切进去，切进去。车头切进去。
Come on, get in. Get in. Nose in.

449
00:29:16,640 --> 00:29:18,870
前轮现在给我抓住地啊！
Give it some front-end grip now!

450
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:31,993
感觉不错！
It's good!

451
00:29:37,520 --> 00:29:38,874
要糟！
It's bad!

452
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,349
救回来了！
All right!

453
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:50,560
噢，爽！
Oh, yeah!

454
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:58,671
<i>我想买一辆这车。</i>
<i>I want one of these cars.</i>

455
00:29:58,760 --> 00:30:01,400
不，等等，我想买这么一个湖。
No, wait, I want one of these lakes.

456
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:05,997
最后一个开阔的大长弯。
The final big, sweeping corner.

457
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:09,954
<i>我知道，裁判们想看点优雅的、
漂亮的东西。</i>
<i>They're looking, I know,
for something elegant, something pretty.</i>

458
00:30:11,240 --> 00:30:12,230
哇噢！
Whoa!

459
00:30:19,640 --> 00:30:21,199
-詹姆斯！
-非常棒。
-James!
-Very good.

460
00:30:21,280 --> 00:30:22,475
我赢了！
I won!

461
00:30:22,600 --> 00:30:24,398
<i>-你说你赢了是什么意思？
-我赢了！</i>
<i>-What do you mean, you won?
- Iwon!</i>

462
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:27,279
<i>得了吧。我跑那一圈
只用了2分03秒。</i>
<i>No, come on. I went round there
in two minutes, three seconds.</i>

463
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:30,876
你撞车的时候，
其实已经落后整整30秒了。
You were actually 30 seconds behind
when you crashed.

464
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:33,469
听着，花样滑冰又不是跟秒表赛跑。
Look, ice dancing is not against the clock.

465
00:30:33,560 --> 00:30:36,632
比的是姿态、精妙和美感。
而我显然比你……
It's about poise and delicacy and beauty.
And I was much more...

466
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,352
美得多。
beautiful than you were.

467
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:42,990
是，但我们这就是计时的，
而且这证明了四轮驱动
Yes, but this is against the clock
and it proves that four-wheel drive

468
00:30:43,080 --> 00:30:47,074
彻底把两驱给虐出翔了。
到此为止，这是我的胜利。
has thrashed two-wheel drive.
That's the end of it. That was my victory.

469
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:50,155
天快黑了，我们没工夫再吵下去了，行吧？
It's going dark, so we don't have
any more time to argue, okay?

470
00:30:50,240 --> 00:30:51,639
而且重点是，
And the thing is

471
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:55,350
在他深陷于奇形怪状的蔬菜世界之前，
that before he became mired in a world
of amusing shaped vegetables,

472
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:59,115
理查德·哈蒙德曾和詹姆斯
一起来挪威跑过一场比赛。
Richard Hammond came to Norway
with James for a race.

473
00:30:59,200 --> 00:31:01,635
没错，所以我们觉得
应该带大家再重温一次。
Yes, and we thought
we'd show it to you again.

474
00:31:02,040 --> 00:31:03,678
-那么……
-但在那之前……
-Now...
-But just before...

475
00:31:03,760 --> 00:31:06,274
<i>快去开你的“发现”过来，
我得把这车给拖出来。</i>
<i>Go and get your Discovery
'cause I need to pull this out.</i>

476
00:31:06,360 --> 00:31:08,431
-能先给你看个东西吗？
-啥？
-Can I show you something first?
-What?

477
00:31:08,520 --> 00:31:10,796
既然刚才聊到了理查德·哈蒙德，
Since we were talking about
Richard Hammond,

478
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:12,632
你的车好像也刚去美白了牙齿。
your car's had its teeth whitened.

479
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:14,074
（两人大笑）
(BOTH LAUGHING)

480
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:21,676
哈蒙德：利勒哈默尔拥有
全世界最险峻的雪车赛道之一。
RICHARD: Lillehammer has one of the most
formidable bobsleigh runs in the world.

481
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:26,755
这条九曲十八弯的下坡赛道
全长将近两公里。
The downhill course of twists and turns
stretches for almost two kilometres.

482
00:31:38,040 --> 00:31:41,271
即便如此，一支顶尖的有舵雪橇队
冲下这条赛道
Even so, a crack bobsleigh team
can get down this run

483
00:31:41,360 --> 00:31:42,873
也只需不到一分钟，
in just under a minute,

484
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:46,112
<i>而且雪橇本身的时速
能飚到80英里。</i>
<i>with the bobsleigh itself
hitting 80 miles an hour.</i>

485
00:31:46,520 --> 00:31:49,114
不过，这极致的速度
是要让乘员付出代价的，
The speed comes at a price
for the passengers, though,

486
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:51,191
因为雪橇队里的每个人
because each member
of the bobsleigh team

487
00:31:51,280 --> 00:31:54,636
都得承受高达5G的过弯横向重力。
is subjected to cornering forces of 5G.

488
00:31:54,720 --> 00:31:56,950
这比F1赛车手承受的还要凶残。
That's more than an F1 driver suffers.

489
00:31:57,400 --> 00:32:00,597
说实话，干这事儿你非得够勇、够傻，
Honestly, to do this
you'd have to be brave, stupid

490
00:32:00,680 --> 00:32:03,593
或者纯粹是想上电视想疯了。
or just desperate to get on the television.

491
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:06,400
所以，我就坐这儿了，
正中间这位置。
So this is where I'll be sitting,
here in the middle.

492
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:10,155
为了把难度拉满，
我们还要搞一场竞速对决。
And to make things even more arduous,
we're gonna have a race.

493
00:32:12,160 --> 00:32:15,073
我们特地跑到利勒哈默尔，是因为在雪橇滑道旁，
We've come to Lillehammer
because alongside the bobsleigh run,

494
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:16,559
刚好有这么一条公路。
we have this road.

495
00:32:16,640 --> 00:32:19,075
它们起点完全相同，一路盘旋下山，
They start in the same place,
they run down the hill,

496
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:21,071
终点也在同一个地方。
and they finish in the same place.

497
00:32:21,720 --> 00:32:25,076
詹姆斯：这条公路的长度
几乎跟雪橇滑道一模一样。
JAMES: The road is almost exactly
the same length as the bob run.

498
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:29,831
而且跟滑道一样，路面湿滑、危机四伏，
到处都是刁钻的发卡弯。
And like the bob run, it's slippery,
dangerous and full of difficult corners.

499
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:33,590
这需要一台狠角色才搞得定。
It requires a special vehicle.

500
00:32:38,560 --> 00:32:40,198
于是我们弄来了这台大家伙。
So that's what we've got.

501
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:42,920
一台三菱Evo世界拉力锦标赛战车，
It's a Mitsubishi Evo world rally car,

502
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:46,550
拥有300匹马力的涡轮增压发动机、全时四驱系统，
with a 300 horsepower
turbocharged engine, four-wheel drive

503
00:32:46,640 --> 00:32:48,278
以及全套带钉雪地胎。
and studded tyres.

504
00:32:49,280 --> 00:32:52,750
所以挑战来了：
拉力赛车能跑赢有舵雪橇吗？
So that's the challenge.
Can the rally car beat the bobsleigh?

505
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:57,118
我坚信它绝对能赢，
虽说哈蒙德咬定我绝无胜算。
I happen to think it can, although
Hammond tells me it definitely can't.

506
00:32:58,400 --> 00:32:59,629
理查德：这是我的雪橇滑道。
RICHARD: This is my bobsleigh run.

507
00:32:59,720 --> 00:33:02,633
从这儿出发，一路扭啊扭滑到这儿，终点在那儿。
It starts here and it wiggles
all the way down here and it finishes there.

508
00:33:02,920 --> 00:33:04,957
詹姆斯：这条绿色的则是公路，
JAMES: And this is the road,
which is in green,

509
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:06,917
也是从这儿出发，一路蜿蜒盘旋到那儿。
and it starts here and it wiggles
all the way up there.

510
00:33:07,000 --> 00:33:08,832
但终点完全是同一个地方。
But it finishes in exactly the same place.

511
00:33:08,920 --> 00:33:10,354
对，但关键问题在这儿。
Yes, but here's a point.

512
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:13,239
我的雪橇从起点一路冲到底，
My bobsleigh can get from there
all the way down to there

513
00:33:13,320 --> 00:33:15,118
用时不到一分钟。你死定了。
in less than a minute. You've had it.

514
00:33:15,200 --> 00:33:18,636
可你瞧，你从那儿到那儿
靠的仅仅是地心引力。
But, you see, all you've got to take you
from there to there is gravity.

515
00:33:18,720 --> 00:33:20,119
-对啊。
-那算个屁。
-Yes.
-That's nothing.

516
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:23,318
我可是有足足300匹马力、大号涡轮，
Well, I've got 300 horsepower
and a huge turbocharger

517
00:33:23,400 --> 00:33:25,789
每条轮胎上还有420根防滑钢钉，
and 420 spikes in each tyre

518
00:33:25,880 --> 00:33:27,996
再加上地心引力带我冲下去。
and gravity to get down there.

519
00:33:28,080 --> 00:33:31,072
得了吧，我的雪橇生来就是跑冰面的。
Yes, but my bobsleigh was custom built
for going on ice.

520
00:33:31,160 --> 00:33:33,959
而你那台车不过是靠着
特制雪地胎之类的玩意儿临时改装的。
Your car has had to be sort of
adapted with clever tyres and stuff.

521
00:33:34,040 --> 00:33:35,474
<i>- 你穿的是紧身裤吧。
- 没错。</i>
<i>-You're wearing tights.
- I am.</i>

522
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:38,154
我可没法听一个穿紧身裤的男人
跟我讲物理。
I can't take lectures on physics
from a man in tights.

523
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:41,232
<i>- 我知道我穿了紧身裤。
- 跳芭蕾还行，讲物理？算了吧。</i>
<i>- I am aware of the tights.
-Dancing, yes, but physics, no.</i>

524
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:46,518
詹姆斯：不过说实话，
想跑赢雪车确实难如登天，
JAMES: The truth is, though,
the bob is going to be hard to beat

525
00:33:46,600 --> 00:33:49,160
这基本就意味着
不能由我来开车了。
which kind of counts me out
for driving the car.

526
00:33:52,760 --> 00:33:57,277
所以我们请来了亨宁·索伯格，
挪威全国拉力赛冠军。
So instead we've got Henning Solberg,
the Norwegian National Rally champion.

527
00:33:58,960 --> 00:34:00,598
男子：一、二、三。
MAN: One, two, three.

528
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:04,560
理查德：雪车能不能赢，
全看起跑推得怎么样。
RICHARD: The bobsleigh's chance of victory
all depends on how good our start is.

529
00:34:04,640 --> 00:34:06,677
这意味着我和挪威冬奥雪车队
That means intense preparation for me

530
00:34:06,760 --> 00:34:08,671
必须展开高强度特训。
and the Norwegian Olympic
Bobsleigh team.

531
00:34:08,760 --> 00:34:09,750
一，二。
One, two.

532
00:34:12,040 --> 00:34:17,035
我们在苦练冲刺，
而舵手则在脑海里默默盘算整条赛道。
And while we practise running,
the driver visualises the course in his head.

533
00:34:21,240 --> 00:34:24,995
这一切全成了懒癌晚期梅的笑料，
看乐了他。
All of this provided
much merriment for the bone-idle May.

534
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:26,912
- 你在热身吗？
- 是啊。
-Are you warming up?
-Yes.

535
00:34:27,000 --> 00:34:28,798
我也在“热身”呢。
I'm warming up as well.

536
00:34:29,920 --> 00:34:32,389
老实说，我可一点都笑不出来，
To be honest, I couldn't see
the funny side of it

537
00:34:32,480 --> 00:34:35,438
因为我真的很怕拖了大家的后腿。
because I was really worried
about letting the team down.

538
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:41,553
在这里耽误哪怕一秒，
到了终点就会被放大成三倍。
Any time you lose here, a second
is multiplied by three at the bottom.

539
00:34:41,640 --> 00:34:43,313
那就是整整落后三秒。
So that'll be three seconds.

540
00:34:43,400 --> 00:34:46,677
而且我也担心自己的小身板吃不消。
And I was also worried about
whether my body would cope.

541
00:34:46,760 --> 00:34:48,910
最关键的是进弯的时候，
The key thing is, as you go into the corners,

542
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:51,594
得屏住呼吸，尽可能深吸一口气憋住，
to hold your breath,
to get as much breath in as you can

543
00:34:51,680 --> 00:34:53,398
因为这样才能撑住你的身体。
'cause that actually holds your body up.

544
00:34:53,480 --> 00:34:56,472
在弯道承受巨大G值时，它能保护你。
It supports you when you're being
subjected to G forces in the corners.

545
00:34:56,560 --> 00:35:00,349
据说在下面有几个地方，G值会飙到6.5G。
Apparently, in a couple of places
down there, it hits 6.5G.

546
00:35:00,960 --> 00:35:02,951
舵手跟我说他滑了六年雪车，
The driver told me
he's been doing this six years

547
00:35:03,040 --> 00:35:05,350
身高生生被压矮了三公分。
and he's three centimetres shorter.

548
00:35:06,480 --> 00:35:08,391
我可再也矮不起三公分了。
I can't afford to lose three centimetres.

549
00:35:13,440 --> 00:35:16,717
詹姆斯系好了安全带，我也准备就绪。
James was strapped in
and I was ready to run.

550
00:35:18,960 --> 00:35:21,839
我们的拉力车手几乎一句英文都不会讲，
Our race rally driver
could hardly speak any English,

551
00:35:21,920 --> 00:35:25,800
<i>但这丝毫不妨碍詹姆斯
摆出一副高高在上的英式腔调给他做赛前动员。</i>
<i>but that didn't stop James
giving him a patronising British pep talk.</i>

552
00:35:26,200 --> 00:35:30,478
听好了，亨宁，内燃机工业的声誉
Righto, Henning, it's the reputation
of internal combustion

553
00:35:30,560 --> 00:35:32,233
可全都压在你肩上了，
resting on your shoulders

554
00:35:33,360 --> 00:35:35,033
就在接下来的一分钟里。
in the next minute or so.

555
00:35:37,440 --> 00:35:40,353
詹姆斯：我打算用我心爱的秒表给车计时。
JAMES: I was going to time the car
with my trusty stopwatch.

556
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:43,671
而哈蒙德的雪车则由赛道裁判来计时。
And Hammond's bob would be timed
by the course officials.

557
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:45,872
理查德：成败在此一举！
RICHARD: This was it

558
00:36:03,520 --> 00:36:06,114
看着点树，你个疯子！
Mind the trees, you nutter!

559
00:36:06,960 --> 00:36:09,076
理查德：开始进弯了！
RICHARD: We're starting to turn.

560
00:36:09,160 --> 00:36:12,994
进弯了！拐过去了！一共16个弯……
That's a turn! That's a turn. 16 corners...

561
00:36:13,720 --> 00:36:15,791
现在已经搞定三个弯了。
Now that's three of them done.

562
00:36:18,760 --> 00:36:21,559
詹姆斯：一分钟要在冰面上跑完两公里。
JAMES: Two kilometres on ice in a minute.

563
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:24,116
老天，亨宁这下可有得拼了。
Boy, has Henning got it all to do.

564
00:36:24,920 --> 00:36:27,309
哎哟，疼死我了！撞到头了。
Ooh, that hurts a lot That's my head.

565
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:29,790
（哔——）
(BLEEP)

566
00:36:31,080 --> 00:36:35,551
<i>理查德：雪车起步可能慢了点，
但后头简直越来越快。</i>
<i>RICHARD: The bob may have started slow,
but it was just getting faster and faster.</i>

567
00:36:35,640 --> 00:36:38,234
而且这帮家伙根本就不踩刹车！
And these guys never use the brakes.

568
00:36:38,880 --> 00:36:40,279
<i>别、别、别，不要啊！</i>
<i>No, no, no, not!</i>

569
00:36:41,600 --> 00:36:44,194
前面是一组组合弯道……
噢，过了一个。
Now there's a complex coming up...
Oh, that's one.

570
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,518
又来一个！
And there's another.

571
00:36:47,040 --> 00:36:50,954
赛程过半，冲过一千米时，
谁赢谁输还真说不准。
At midpoint, 1,000 metres in,
it was anybody's guess.

572
00:36:53,200 --> 00:36:55,157
詹姆斯：好家伙……踩刹车啊，老兄！
JAMES: Right... The brakes, man!

573
00:36:58,920 --> 00:37:01,196
（尖叫声）
(SHOUTING)

574
00:37:01,280 --> 00:37:03,078
我脑袋快撞烂了！
I'm banging my head!

575
00:37:08,520 --> 00:37:10,238
（沉闷的心跳声）
(MUFFLED HEART BEATING)

576
00:37:18,640 --> 00:37:20,711
嗷，我的头！颠死我了！
Oh, my head! Big bumps!

577
00:37:22,120 --> 00:37:23,997
詹姆斯：亨宁简直神了。
JAMES: Henning was just awesome.

578
00:37:24,080 --> 00:37:26,799
在冰面上根本不可能开这么快！
You can't go this fast on ice.

579
00:37:27,040 --> 00:37:28,314
（哔——）
(BLEEP)

580
00:37:29,600 --> 00:37:32,069
他蹭到边了！他要谋杀我们啊！
He hit the side! He's going to kill us!

581
00:37:36,560 --> 00:37:38,358
我可不想穿着紧身衣死掉！
I don't want to die in tights!

582
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:55,949
59秒68。
59:68.

583
00:37:57,240 --> 00:37:59,470
我们赢了吗？他跑了多少？
Did we win? What did he do?

584
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:04,712
天哪。
God.

585
00:38:04,800 --> 00:38:05,915
我整个人都要散架了。
I'm broken.

586
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:07,991
-你们跑了多少？
-59秒68。
-What have you done it in?
-59:68.

587
00:38:08,640 --> 00:38:10,836
快点，快揭晓吧。
Come on. Come on, come on.

588
00:38:11,920 --> 00:38:15,072
-1分02秒24。
-我们赢啦！
-1:02:24.
-We won!

589
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:17,712
我们做到了！
We did it!

590
00:38:18,360 --> 00:38:21,432
<i>兄弟们好样的！呃，但愿我没
给你们拖后腿。</i>
<i>The boys! Well, I hope I didn't
slow you up too much.</i>

591
00:38:21,520 --> 00:38:23,079
-太牛了。
-是啊。
-That was fantastic.
-Yeah.

592
00:38:23,160 --> 00:38:25,549
我们赢了。这趟真是绝了。
We did it. That really was something.

593
00:38:25,800 --> 00:38:28,110
太赞了。漂亮！
Awesome. Yes!

594
00:38:31,840 --> 00:38:35,515
好了，那是去年的事，现在言归正传，
而且我带来一个好消息。
Right, that was last year, this is now,
and I have some good news.

595
00:38:35,760 --> 00:38:39,276
恰逢周末，理查德·哈蒙德
终于能够成功脱身，
It's the weekend and Richard Hammond
has therefore been able to escape

596
00:38:39,360 --> 00:38:43,672
从他那些奇形怪状的薯片世界里逃出来了，
而且他今天来到了现场！
from his world of amusingly shaped
potato crisps and he's here!

597
00:38:46,400 --> 00:38:50,473
理查德：在此之前，铃木最为人熟知的
是造小型越野车，
RICHARD: Up until now, Suzuki has been
well-known for making small jeeps

598
00:38:50,560 --> 00:38:52,836
以及他们的“廉价车”。
and their reasonably priced cars.

599
00:38:53,200 --> 00:38:56,830
至于他们造的其他所有玩意儿，
无趣程度基本就跟那棵松树差不多。
Everything else they've made
is about as interesting as that pine tree.

600
00:38:57,640 --> 00:39:00,473
呃，不对，可能是那边那棵。
中间的那一棵。
Well, no, maybe that one there.
That one in the middle there.

601
00:39:04,240 --> 00:39:07,710
但现在，他们冷不丁地
搞出了这么个玩意儿——
But now, out of nowhere,
they've come up with this,

602
00:39:07,800 --> 00:39:09,074
全新雨燕。
the new Swift

603
00:39:09,160 --> 00:39:11,310
我真的是说“毫无征兆”。
And I do mean out of nowhere.

604
00:39:11,400 --> 00:39:13,311
瞧瞧它这模样。
Just look at it.

605
00:39:13,400 --> 00:39:14,879
当这玩意儿开过去时，
When this thing drives past,

606
00:39:14,960 --> 00:39:17,315
你还真会忍不住回头多瞅两眼，
对吧？
you really are going to give it
a second glance, aren't you?

607
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:20,789
它售价还不到八千英镑，
It costs less than eight grand,

608
00:39:20,880 --> 00:39:24,157
可就花这点钱，你就能拥有一台挺活泛的
1.3升发动机，
and yet for that, you get a perky
1.3 litre engine,

609
00:39:24,240 --> 00:39:28,791
CD播放机、电动后视镜、防眩隐私玻璃，
还有几个安全气囊。
CD player, electric mirrors, tinted glass
and some airbags.

610
00:39:32,400 --> 00:39:35,199
它做到了微型车
最精妙的一点。
It does just about the cleverest thing
a small car can do.

611
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:37,430
那就是——开起来完全不像辆小车。
Which is, not feel like a small car.

612
00:39:37,520 --> 00:39:39,591
感觉敦实厚重，很有分量。
It feels big and solid.

613
00:39:39,680 --> 00:39:41,193
而且显得相当成熟。
And it feels grown up.

614
00:39:41,280 --> 00:39:45,069
考虑到我们接下来要拿它干的事，
这绝对是件大好事。
Which, considering what we're about
to do with it is a good thing.

615
00:39:45,160 --> 00:39:47,800
要知道，上回我们测微型车的时候，
You see, the last time
we tested a small car,

616
00:39:47,960 --> 00:39:50,839
最后演变成了开着10辆车去踢足球。
we ended up playing football
with 10 of them.

617
00:39:56,920 --> 00:40:01,198
那次用的是丰田Aygo，
而且坦白讲，最后搞得一片狼藉。
They were Toyota Aygos
and, frankly, it all got a bit messy.

618
00:40:02,360 --> 00:40:05,512
问题是，眼下这种天气
Thing is, it is a bit nippy for football

619
00:40:05,600 --> 00:40:07,750
踢足球实在有点冻屁股。
in these conditions.

620
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:09,953
但别灰心……
But don't despair...

621
00:40:18,200 --> 00:40:20,840
因为我们可以玩这个。
because we can do this.

622
00:40:21,920 --> 00:40:25,675
我宣布，Top Gear冬季奥运会
I declare the Top Gear Winter Olympics

623
00:40:25,760 --> 00:40:29,594
铃木雨燕汽车冰球锦标……
Suzuki Swift Car Ice Hockey "Cha”

624
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:30,715
开幕！
open/

625
00:40:33,920 --> 00:40:35,957
哈蒙德：没错，这就是赛场，
RICHARD: Yes, this is the pitch

626
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:39,230
这就是参赛队员。
and these are the players.

627
00:40:39,320 --> 00:40:42,597
十辆铃木雨燕，打五人制对抗赛。
Ten Suzuki Swifts, making it five a side.

628
00:40:42,680 --> 00:40:45,354
全部由当地的拉力赛车手掌舵。
All piloted by local rally drivers.

629
00:40:46,080 --> 00:40:50,631
<i>詹姆斯和我分别担任两队队长，
杰里米当裁判。</i>
<i>James and I would be team captains
and Jeremy the ref.</i>

630
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:52,513
哈蒙德：听着，这规则一点不难。
RICHARD: Look, it's not difficult.

631
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:55,956
冰球基本上称得上
全世界最暴力的运动了。
Ice hockey is basically
the most violent sport in the world.

632
00:40:56,040 --> 00:40:59,317
-绝无例外。所以……
-所以要是你咬了詹姆斯……
-Bar none. So...
-So if you bite James...

633
00:40:59,400 --> 00:41:01,118
<i>哦对，不是，那个……
我是说，要是真闹到……</i>
<i>Oh, yeah. No, that...
I mean, if it gets really...</i>

634
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:03,350
要是出了人命，
If there is a death,

635
00:41:03,440 --> 00:41:05,272
那你就必须把肇事者关进受罚席。
then you have to put somebody
in the sin bin.

636
00:41:05,360 --> 00:41:07,749
<i>-那时候我才吹号？
-对，要是场面彻底失控打成一团的话。</i>
<i>-And that's when I blow my horn?
-Yes, if it all goes really nasty.</i>

637
00:41:07,840 --> 00:41:09,911
<i>-要是我得叫停比赛，就吹这个？
-没错。</i>
<i>-If I have stop the game, I blow this?
-Yes.</i>

638
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:12,116
-所以就是……
-只要你……
-So it's...
-Just you...

639
00:41:14,240 --> 00:41:16,197
喇叭头儿掉下来了。
The end's come off.

640
00:41:16,280 --> 00:41:20,638
<i>哈蒙德：看台上已是座无虚席、人山人海，
巨型冰球也已就位，</i>
<i>RICHARD: With the stands packed
to the rafters and the giant puck in place,</i>

641
00:41:20,720 --> 00:41:22,358
我们准备开球了。
we were ready for the off.

642
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:26,030
好了，蓝队，
由“慢队长”领衔！
Okay, the blue team,
captained by Captain Slow!

643
00:41:26,120 --> 00:41:27,758
这代表“黄金档电视”！
That's Primetime television.

644
00:41:27,840 --> 00:41:31,799
红队，队长是
理查德·菲利普·斯科菲尔德·哈蒙德！
The red team, captained by
Richard Phillip Schofield Hammond/

645
00:41:31,880 --> 00:41:34,394
这代表“白天档电视”！我们准备好了！
That's Daytime television! We're ready!

646
00:41:34,840 --> 00:41:36,069
（吹响气喇叭）
(BLOWING AIR HORN)

647
00:41:53,240 --> 00:41:56,073
詹姆斯：不到一分钟，
“白天档”就进球了。
JAMES: Within a minute,
Daytime TV scored.

648
00:41:57,560 --> 00:41:58,630
球进啦！
Goal!

649
00:41:58,720 --> 00:42:01,280
冰球里也叫“进球”吗？对。
Is it a "goal" in ice hockey? Yeah.

650
00:42:08,880 --> 00:42:11,269
话说当年我们这么玩的时候，
撞车事故可多了去了，
Now, there were a lot of crashes
when we did this

651
00:42:11,360 --> 00:42:13,112
那时是用Aygo踢足球。
with the Aygos playing football.

652
00:42:13,200 --> 00:42:17,319
我觉得把比赛搬到冰面上，
安全系数大大提高了。
I think by putting it on ice,
we've made it a lot safer.

653
00:42:24,000 --> 00:42:26,719
詹姆斯：虽然我嘴里飙着各种足球解说套话……
JAMES: Despite my best football clichés...

654
00:42:26,800 --> 00:42:28,598
噢，他像三文鱼一样高高跃起！
Oh, he's up like a salmon.

655
00:42:28,680 --> 00:42:31,035
我们单刀直入直奔球门。
经典的二过一配合！
We're on a clear run for goal.
It's the old one-two.

656
00:42:32,120 --> 00:42:34,634
詹姆斯：“黄金档队”
却早已乱成了一锅粥。
JAMES: Team Primetime
were all over the place.

657
00:42:34,720 --> 00:42:35,915
打偏了！
It's gone wide.

658
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:40,713
理查德：与此同时，
“白天档”手感火热。
RICHARD: Meanwhile,
Daytime TV were on fire.

659
00:42:40,800 --> 00:42:43,713
尽管裁判明显在拉偏架……
And despite an obviously biased ref...

660
00:42:43,800 --> 00:42:47,191
杰里米：加油啊，詹姆斯！
上啊哥们儿，机会来了！
JEREMY: Come on, James!
Come on, man, you've got it!

661
00:42:48,800 --> 00:42:50,950
理查德：……但我们还是轰进了第二球。
RICHARD: banged home goal two.

662
00:42:51,040 --> 00:42:52,235
球进啦！
Goal!

663
00:42:53,200 --> 00:42:56,591
紧接着第三球也应声入网。
And goal three in quick succession.

664
00:42:56,680 --> 00:42:58,876
伙计们，现在谁才是黄金档啊？！
Who's primetime now, then, boys?

665
00:42:58,960 --> 00:43:00,075
（欢呼声）
(WHOOPING)

666
00:43:00,160 --> 00:43:02,549
詹姆斯：没错，我的队伍正在被无情痛宰。
JAMES: Yes, my team were being trounced.

667
00:43:02,640 --> 00:43:04,916
而当我们好不容易进了一球，
And when we finally did score,

668
00:43:06,320 --> 00:43:08,072
猜猜谁正忙着干别的事？
guess who was otherwise engaged?

669
00:43:11,680 --> 00:43:15,310
没错，总而言之，这位裁判对比赛的掌控
简直烂透了。
Yes, all in all, the ref's grasp
of the game was poor.

670
00:43:16,440 --> 00:43:18,238
-怎么会这样？
-这个嘛……
-Why has that happened?
-Well, that's...

671
00:43:18,320 --> 00:43:20,152
还有，你们怎么还没进球？
And why haven't you scored?

672
00:43:20,240 --> 00:43:22,516
-我们进球了。
-反正我没看见。
-We have scored.
-Well, I haven't seen it.

673
00:43:22,600 --> 00:43:25,069
不对，我们刚才刚进的！到底谁是裁判啊？！
No, we just scored then. Who's the referee?

674
00:43:25,520 --> 00:43:26,874
<i>-我刚才稍微滑倒了一下。
-是吗？</i>
<i>- I fell over a bit.
-Did you?</i>

675
00:43:26,960 --> 00:43:28,598
<i>-你漏看了进球？
-我漏看了进球。</i>
<i>-You missed the goal?
- Imissed the goal.</i>

676
00:43:28,680 --> 00:43:30,273
只要没吹哨判定，那就不算进球。
If it's not declared, it's not a goal.

677
00:43:30,360 --> 00:43:31,509
你愿不愿意相信我的话——
Are you prepared to accept my word

678
00:43:31,600 --> 00:43:33,955
以我黄金档电视主持人的信誉起誓，
我们刚才进了个极其漂亮的好球？
as a primetime television presenter
that we scored a superb goal?

679
00:43:34,040 --> 00:43:35,439
-愿意，我相信。
-很好。谢谢裁判。
-Yes, I am.
-Good. Thank you, ref.

680
00:43:35,520 --> 00:43:37,716
<i>-但我其实真没看着。
-噢，得了吧！</i>
<i>-But I didn't actually see it.
-Oh, come on!</i>

681
00:43:37,800 --> 00:43:40,076
哈蒙德：不过“白天组”依然
领先两球，
RICHARD: Daytime were still
two goals ahead, though,

682
00:43:40,160 --> 00:43:42,071
裁判（杰里米）可看不顺眼了。
and the ref didn't like that

683
00:43:42,200 --> 00:43:43,554
你搞……
what you...

684
00:43:43,640 --> 00:43:45,039
球在正中间！
It's in the middle.

685
00:43:48,400 --> 00:43:50,755
<i>哈蒙德：詹姆斯立刻
捡了大便宜。</i>
<i>RICHARD: James took
immediate advantage.</i>

686
00:43:50,880 --> 00:43:52,029
冲啊，小伙子们！
Come on, boys!

687
00:43:52,920 --> 00:43:54,479
上啊，三号，三号，快上！
Come on, three, three, three!

688
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:57,354
进了！漂亮！
That's in. That's lovely.

689
00:43:57,440 --> 00:43:59,238
球进啦！
Goal!

690
00:43:59,320 --> 00:44:01,277
他真棒，不是吗？
给他个大喇叭，他就乐开花了。
He's great, isn't he?
Give him a megaphone, he's happy.

691
00:44:03,720 --> 00:44:05,472
加油，比约恩和比约恩！
Come on, Bjorn and Bjorn.

692
00:44:08,240 --> 00:44:11,392
哈蒙德：但没过多久，
詹姆斯就撞上了自家队友，
RICHARD: But moments later,
James crashed into his own man,

693
00:44:11,480 --> 00:44:13,994
把自个儿球门大喇喇地敞给了我。
leaving his goalmouth wide open for me.

694
00:44:18,520 --> 00:44:20,716
（哀嚎）
(HOWLING)

695
00:44:23,160 --> 00:44:25,674
<i>哈蒙德：打那之后，
比赛彻底进入了白热化。</i>
<i>RICHARD: After that,
the match really hotted up.</i>

696
00:44:27,320 --> 00:44:29,118
至少对绝大多数人来说是这样。
For most people, that is.

697
00:44:29,200 --> 00:44:30,952
哟，那是啤酒吗？
Oh, is that a beer?

698
00:44:42,360 --> 00:44:43,350
（欢呼）
(WHOOPING)

699
00:44:46,920 --> 00:44:48,354
噢，完了。是哈蒙德。
Oh, no. It's Hammond.

700
00:44:48,440 --> 00:44:49,669
真是见鬼了，詹姆斯。
Bloody hell, James.

701
00:44:50,360 --> 00:44:53,796
哈蒙德：不管怎样，“白天组”再下一城，
现在的比分是……
RICHARD: Still, another goal for Daytime,
making the score...

702
00:44:54,440 --> 00:44:58,115
现在是五比二？还是三？啥情况？
That is now 5-2? 3? What?

703
00:44:58,840 --> 00:45:00,319
到底几比几啊？
What is it?

704
00:45:03,400 --> 00:45:05,596
哈蒙德：随着比赛
进入最后尾声，
RICHARD: As the game
entered its final stages,

705
00:45:05,680 --> 00:45:08,513
场上的暴力程度
总算达到了正统冰球赛的水准。
the violence reached
proper ice hockey levels.

706
00:45:09,440 --> 00:45:11,351
撞到自己人了，不过别往心里去。
Struck me own bloke, but never mind.

707
00:45:11,960 --> 00:45:15,919
<i>不得不说，事实证明
这些雨燕真是皮实抗造的小铁车。</i>
<i>These are proving themselves to be
Tough little cars, these Swifts, I must say.</i>

708
00:45:18,280 --> 00:45:19,759
翻车了！底朝天了！
Upside down!

709
00:45:20,280 --> 00:45:21,918
（惨叫）
(HOWLING)

710
00:45:22,920 --> 00:45:25,070
那一下估计摔得够呛。
That could be where he banged himself.

711
00:45:25,160 --> 00:45:26,878
男子：你们有吸尘器吗？
MAN: Do you have any vacuum cleaner?

712
00:45:26,960 --> 00:45:29,839
-吸尘器？
-男子：对，清理座椅。
-A vacuum cleaner?
-MAN: Yes, clean the seats.

713
00:45:29,920 --> 00:45:33,151
<i>《Top Gear》剧组会有吸尘器？做梦。</i>
<i>Does Top Gear have a vacuum cleaner? No.</i>

714
00:45:33,480 --> 00:45:35,278
詹姆斯：红队二号车彻底趴窝了，
JAMES: Red 2 was out of action,

715
00:45:35,360 --> 00:45:37,636
但我还没来得及高兴太久。
but my joy was short-lived.

716
00:45:37,840 --> 00:45:39,592
还有备用车！
There is a spare car.

717
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:41,957
我们这会儿正往上面刷“2号”呢。
We're writing number 2 on it as we speak.

718
00:45:42,040 --> 00:45:44,714
比赛还剩最后90秒，
他马上就能重返赛场！
He'll be back in business
with 90 seconds of play left.

719
00:45:44,800 --> 00:45:46,473
裁判，你到底是哪头的啊？
Whose side are you on, ref?

720
00:45:46,560 --> 00:45:50,190
我绝对不偏不倚，
我都把能给的机会全给你了。
I am totally impartial.
I've given you every possible opportunity.

721
00:45:50,280 --> 00:45:52,715
你刚才太让我失望了。
You've just let me down.

722
00:45:52,800 --> 00:45:55,519
扯淡，我可是进了两个精彩绝伦的球，
Rubbish. I've scored two brilliant goals

723
00:45:55,600 --> 00:45:57,511
而你却一直在搭讪
某个挪威女人，
whilst you've been chatting up
some Norwegian woman

724
00:45:57,600 --> 00:45:59,193
还一直杵在酒吧里。
and standing in the bar.

725
00:45:59,280 --> 00:46:01,669
- 那是我老婆。
- 那确实是他老婆。
-That was my wife.
- It was his wife.

726
00:46:07,840 --> 00:46:09,433
理查德：比赛快要结束时，
RICHARD: With play almost over,

727
00:46:09,520 --> 00:46:13,434
我不小心、但极度精准地
把詹姆斯给干翻了。
I accidentally, but very accurately,
took out James.

728
00:46:13,760 --> 00:46:14,795
我出局了！
I'm out!

729
00:46:14,880 --> 00:46:16,712
哈蒙德关小黑屋罚时！
Hammond in the sin bin.

730
00:46:22,120 --> 00:46:24,714
<i>真不敢相信我被关小黑屋了。凭什么啊？</i>
<i>I can't believe I got sin-binned. For what?</i>

731
