00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:55,559
<i>我和詹姆斯顺道去看了看哈蒙德，
视察他堆的防撞雪墙。</i>
<i>James and I dropped in on Hammond
to inspect his snow bank.</i>

866
00:53:56,440 --> 00:53:59,034
<i>我敢打包票，那玩意儿根本刹不住Mini。</i>
<i>I can guarantee that won't stop the Mini.</i>

867
00:53:59,960 --> 00:54:02,952
一方面是因为它根本不够结实，
Partly because it's not substantial enough,

868
00:54:03,040 --> 00:54:07,034
但主要是因为你把它堆在了
那个跳台雪道的正前方，
but mostly because you've built that
in front of that slope,

869
00:54:07,120 --> 00:54:10,112
可Mini要从这一条冲下来啊。
and the Mini is coming down that one.

870
00:54:10,840 --> 00:54:11,830
好吧。
Right.

871
00:54:13,280 --> 00:54:15,715
-行吧。
-杰里米：真是个不折不扣的……
-Righto.
-JEREMY: What a complete...

872
00:54:17,440 --> 00:54:19,113
稍微调整一下就行。
Some adjustments.

873
00:54:19,200 --> 00:54:20,634
就没人通知你吗？
Did nobody tell you?

874
00:54:20,720 --> 00:54:24,600
显然没有！
不然我早就堆在那边了！
No, obviously!
Or I'd have built it over there!

875
00:54:25,840 --> 00:54:27,956
这确实是相当尴尬。
That is fairly embarrassing.

876
00:54:28,040 --> 00:54:31,078
<i>我现在需要一台大家伙。</i>
<i>What I need is a big machine.</i>

877
00:54:33,640 --> 00:54:36,553
理查德：于是我给自己弄来了一台压雪车。
RICHARD: So I got myself a piste basher.

878
00:54:41,360 --> 00:54:45,433
<i>有了它，我非得筑起一道
堪比胡佛水坝的宏伟防线不可。</i>
<i>With this, I am going to construct
something that will rival the Hoover Dam.</i>

879
00:54:45,760 --> 00:54:48,559
那两个笨蛋
这下可笑不出来了。
Those two muppets
will not be laughing at me now.

880
00:54:48,720 --> 00:54:52,839
为了赶进度，
我甚至拉来了一整群拖拉机。
And to speed things up,
I even drafted in a herd of tractors.

881
00:54:58,680 --> 00:55:02,036
杰里米：当菲利普·斯科菲尔德还在
筑造利勒哈默尔的“长城”时……
JEREMY: While Phillip Schofield was
building the great wall of Lillehammer...

882
00:55:02,120 --> 00:55:03,235
哦，没错。
Oh, yeah.

883
00:55:05,960 --> 00:55:10,193
……这辆蓄满了一吨半爆炸推力的
火箭车
...the rocket car, primed with
one and a half tonnes of explosive thrust

884
00:55:10,280 --> 00:55:13,557
踏上了前往跳台顶端的
漫漫长路。
began its long journey
to the top of the jump.

885
00:55:16,760 --> 00:55:21,197
<i>半小时后，冰雪滑槽终于成型，
就等“登山大师”克里斯·波宁顿验收了。</i>
<i>And half an hour later, the ice grooves
were ready for Chris Bonington's approval.</i>

886
00:55:21,280 --> 00:55:22,953
-我没……
-求你别靠我太近。
-I'm not...
-Please don't come near me.

887
00:55:23,040 --> 00:55:25,429
-我没碰你，我没……
-去那边呆着。
-I'm not touching you. I'm not...
-Go over there.

888
00:55:25,520 --> 00:55:27,636
-我离你远着呢。
-那就再好不过了。
-I'm nowhere near you.
-That's really nice.

889
00:55:38,280 --> 00:55:39,554
詹姆斯：这种破事以前可从来没人干过。
JAMES: This has never been done before.

890
00:55:39,640 --> 00:55:42,951
确实没有，事实上在瞎折腾界，
我们已经站在最前沿了。
No. We are in fact at the cutting edge
of cocking about.

891
00:55:45,800 --> 00:55:48,838
杰里米：然而，胡闹的时间
已经结束了。
JEREMY: The time for cocking about,
however, was over.

892
00:55:49,400 --> 00:55:52,836
雪墙筑好了，
目标也标定了，
The wall was finished,
the target was laid down,

893
00:55:52,920 --> 00:55:57,232
姑且算吧，现在一切
都交到火箭专家们的手里了。
sort of, and we were now
in the hands of the rocket men.

894
00:55:59,720 --> 00:56:01,791
他们正在给火箭加注燃料。
They're filling the rockets with fuel.

895
00:56:01,880 --> 00:56:03,678
我们得把那个最大排放量压下来。
We need to get that maximum
emission down.

896
00:56:03,760 --> 00:56:05,159
马上处理，好。
Straight away, yeah.

897
00:56:05,240 --> 00:56:06,992
理查德：待会儿绝对会
是一场惨绝人寰的大混乱。
RICHARD: It's going to be
an appalling mess.

898
00:56:07,080 --> 00:56:09,230
大爆炸，大爆炸，
一辆起火的Mini……
An explosion. An explosion.
A burning Mini...

899
00:56:09,320 --> 00:56:11,231
-惨不忍睹。
-……四脚朝天地砸下来。
-Carnage.
-...coming down on its roof.

900
00:56:11,320 --> 00:56:15,518
正在泄压。红、白、蓝。
Venting. Red, white, blue.

901
00:56:15,600 --> 00:56:17,238
-确认。
-确认泄压。
-Confirm.
-Confirm venting.

902
00:56:18,080 --> 00:56:21,789
倒数三、二、一，排空。
And in three, two, one, purge.

903
00:56:22,360 --> 00:56:23,475
冲啊，Mini！
Come on, Mini!

904
00:56:24,040 --> 00:56:28,716
已就绪。五、四、三、二，
Armed. Five, four, three, two,

905
00:56:28,840 --> 00:56:30,558
一。发射。
one. Initiate.

906
00:56:45,520 --> 00:56:46,669
（众人欢呼）
(ALL CHEERING)

907
00:56:48,360 --> 00:56:49,953
那堵雪墙马上就要派上用场了！
The wall's going to be needed!

908
00:56:51,120 --> 00:56:52,633
（众人大笑）
(ALL LAUGHING)

909
00:56:53,880 --> 00:56:56,872
-我们差了一截。
-我们没超过跳台滑雪选手。
-We were a bit short.
-We didn't beat the ski jumper.

910
00:56:56,960 --> 00:56:58,553
它滑雪滑得怎样？
How well did it ski?

911
00:57:05,160 --> 00:57:07,310
杰里米：滑得漂亮极了！
JEREMY: It's brilliant skiing!

912
00:57:11,520 --> 00:57:15,229
我已经很满意了，反正就这样吧，
我得撤了。
I'm satisfied with that
and anyway, that's it, I have to go.

913
00:57:15,320 --> 00:57:17,311
我得回我的日间电视节目圈去了。
I have to go back
to the world of daytime telly.

914
00:57:17,400 --> 00:57:20,074
-兄弟们，玩得很开心，再见！
-你能来真是太棒了。
-Boys, it's been a joy. Goodbye.
-It's been great having you here.

915
00:57:20,160 --> 00:57:21,912
-感谢捧场。
-刚才真是不一般。
-Thanks for coming.
-That was quite something.

916
00:57:22,000 --> 00:57:23,035
拜拜。
Bye.

917
00:57:23,120 --> 00:57:25,999
其实我们也可以撤了，
因为这期节目已经到底了。
Actually, we can go anyway
'cause it's the end of the show.

918
00:57:26,120 --> 00:57:28,589
不，还没完，还有最后一件事。
No, it isn't. There's one more thing.

919
00:57:31,840 --> 00:57:33,478
这是一辆雪地摩托。
This is a snowmobile.

920
00:57:33,560 --> 00:57:36,154
基本上就是后头装了坦克履带的
水上摩托艇，
It's a sort of Jet Ski
with a tank frack on the back,

921
00:57:36,240 --> 00:57:38,151
平时是用来放驼鹿的，
and it's used for herding mooses

922
00:57:39,160 --> 00:57:42,710
或者纯粹四处瞎折腾。
但重点来了：
and generally larking about.
But here's the thing.

923
00:57:43,080 --> 00:57:45,515
纵观整个人类历史，
No one in the whole of human history

924
00:57:45,600 --> 00:57:48,592
还从没有任何人尝试过
骑着这玩意儿
has ever attempted
to ride one of these things

925
00:57:48,720 --> 00:57:50,074
从跳台滑雪道上冲下去。
down a ski jump.

926
00:57:52,000 --> 00:57:54,560
至于为什么从没人敢骑雪地摩托
Now the reason why no one has ever
ridden a snowmobile

927
00:57:54,640 --> 00:57:56,392
从那种滑雪跳台上飞下来，
down a ski jump like that,

928
00:57:56,480 --> 00:57:59,359
原因跟我们昨晚没敢往Mini里塞人是一模一样的。
is the same reason we didn't put
anyone in the Mini last night.

929
00:57:59,440 --> 00:58:01,716
没错，因为你八成会被活活摔死。
Yes, 'cause you'd probably
be killed to death.

930
00:58:01,800 --> 00:58:03,279
对，这概率相当大。
Yeah, very good chance of that.

931
00:58:03,360 --> 00:58:06,990
不过万幸的是，
我们认识一个不知恐惧为何物的人。
Luckily, however,
we know a man who has no fear.

932
00:58:07,080 --> 00:58:10,277
你们以为我们把他给忘了？
并没有，他在这儿呢。斯提格！
You thought we'd forgotten him,
but he's here. The Stig.

933
00:58:21,800 --> 00:58:25,634
我最担心的还是落地那一下。
他的蛋蛋啊。
It's the landing I think
I'm worried about most of all. His pods.

934
00:58:46,280 --> 00:58:48,317
在这枚重磅炸弹中，
And on that bombshell,

935
00:58:49,080 --> 00:58:50,753
或者按他现在的嗓音来说，
or as he would now put it,

936
00:58:50,840 --> 00:58:53,070
（捏着尖嗓子）“在这枚重磅炸弹中”，
(IN SQUEAKY VOICE) "On that bombshell",

937
00:58:53,160 --> 00:58:54,514
本期节目也该收尾了。
time to end the show.

938
00:58:54,600 --> 00:58:56,591
非常感谢收看。晚安！
Thanks very much for watching. Good night!

